docs/
research/
# ...EXCEPT the three artifacts src/ LOADS AT RUNTIME. They are tracked JSON (96 KB), not
# build outputs: flood_detect.DETECTOR, flood_exposure.FITS and flood_exposure.COEFFICIENTS
# are module-level `REPO / "research" / ...` constants, so a pod that runs the detector
# reads them off the image. Excluding the whole directory shipped nine waves of images
# without them and nothing could see it - no pod had ever run the flood tick. cloud 14
# ran it and raincheck-live CrashLoopBackOff'd on the first one. The Dockerfile's runtime
# stage COPYs exactly these and LOADS them in its own build assertion, so dropping a line
# here fails the BUILD rather than a pod at 03:00.
!research/flood-09-fits.json
!research/flood-10-coefficients.json
!research/flood-11-detector.json
tests/
.env
**/*.pyc
**/__pycache__/
